Z||000000||XDrewX||06-10-2001||04:10 PM||||I have a haynes manual so i know to use a floor jack on the lower control arms or the center of the cross member.  PROBLEM: my jack wont reach back to any of these points.<BR>doe anyone know of a brand/model of a jack that will reach? i am not going to jack the car up from the sides. ||||reg||4
Z||000001||Leadfoot||06-10-2001||06:31 PM||||I used the factory jack to raise the front until I could get my floor jack under the car.  Since I am always lifting the car to fix something I bought a small jack from PEP Boys.  Works pretty good.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-10-2001||08:25 PM||||I use a small floor jack angled so that the handle reaches just in front of the tire. There's just enough room to work the handle between the tire and fender. <P>This only lifts one side... You'll have to shove a stand under and jack the other side to get both wheels up.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||06-10-2001||08:35 PM||||I drive the front wheels onto a pair of 2x8 blocks of wood when I want to jack up the front end.  The exta height of the tires on the wood gves me enough clearance to operate the jack handle.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
